Building the hexagon_loadlinux firmware
========================================

``pc-bios/hexagon_loadlinux`` is the default firmware for the hexagon
``virt`` machine.  It is the "loadlinux" bootloader from the H2 hypervisor
project: it initializes the H2 hypervisor and jumps to a Linux kernel loaded
at physical address 0xa0000000, passing the device tree blob address in
r1:0.

It is built from the ``roms/hexagon-hypervisor`` submodule with the Hexagon
SDK toolchain.  From the top of that submodule, build H2 itself, then the
loadlinux bootloader that links against it:

  make USE_PKW=0 ARCHV=73 TARGET=opt NULL_ANGEL_TRAP=1 ALL_HTHREADS=1
  make -C linux USE_PKW=0 ARCHV=73 NO_LOAD=1 NULL_ANGEL_TRAP=1 \
      ALL_HTHREADS=1 LINUX_LINK_ADDR=0xa0000000 loadlinux

To rebuild it, ensure ``hexagon-clang`` and ``hexagon-strip`` (from the
`Hexagon SDK <https://softwarecenter.qualcomm.com/catalog/item/Hexagon_SDK>`_)
are on your PATH, then from the top of the QEMU tree run::

  make -C roms hexagon-loadlinux

This updates ``pc-bios/hexagon_loadlinux`` in place.  The image is stripped
of debug info but keeps its ELF program headers so QEMU can load it with
load_elf().
